## All the Ways to Add 1

There are multiple ways to increment a variable in XIOM:

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  var x = 0;

  // Method 1: Full assignment
  x = x + 1;

  // Method 2: Compound assignment
  x += 1;

  return x;
}
```

### The Three Methods

| Method | Syntax | Use Case |
|--------|--------|----------|
| Full assignment | `x = x + 1` | Most explicit, good for beginners |
| Compound assign | `x += 1` | Standard, clean, most common |
| Any amount | `x += n` | Best for non-1 increments |

### Decrement (Subtract 1)

Same patterns, just with subtraction:

```xiom
var count = 10;

count = count - 1;   // 9 — full assignment
count -= 1;          // 8 — compound assignment
```

### By Other Amounts

Compound assignment shines for non-1 increments:

```xiom
var score = 0;
score += 10;   // Add 10 points
score += 50;   // Add 50 bonus

var health = 100;
health -= 25;  // Lose 25 HP
health -= 10;  // Lose 10 more

var size = 1;
size *= 2;     // Double: 2
size *= 2;     // Double: 4
size *= 2;     // Double: 8
```

### In Loops

```xiom
// Counting up
var i = 0;
while i < 10 {
  io.println("Processing...");
  i += 1;  // Clean increment
}

// Counting down
var timer = 10;
while timer > 0 {
  io.println("Ticking...");
  timer -= 1;  // Clean decrement
}
```

### Recommendation

Use `x += 1` as your default increment. It's the standard in most codebases and instantly recognizable.

```xiom
// Preferred — clear, standard, concise
count += 1;

// Also fine — explicit and clear
count = count + 1;
```

